 a sort of complex and protracted  situation so we are working very closely  with these countries so that we can  actually solve this you know protracted  issue think few words to add China and  in Russia they're permanent members of  the Security Council and their voice  could and should be most stronger there  thank you well let me on behalf to thank  our panelists for being with us today  for sharing with us on the very  complicated issue of course the global  community is looking the ways how to  protect the migrants legally how to  protect them operationally because the  biggest gap today the lack of the legacy  the lack of the operation allottee well  how to bring the help in time what to do  with the those who are diving in the  Pacific Indian and Caribbean what to do  with them  there is no way to to protect them from  the UN climate changes how to adapt them  if there is no way how to adopt this  only way to help them to move out who  will cost them what the legal framework  of this hosting  temporary permanently whatever  nationality so  let me know we have two to wish the the  summit in Morocco be successful in LA to  to thank all the participants today and  the dear welcome back for the next  seminars which will be the next semester  only so within the series of global  governments  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

